  "slug": "cryo-cryosiam-ea0d",
  "summary": "Undersampled cryo-EM, HS-AFM and erythrocyte imaging now pair learned priors with sparse or partial data to recover structure.",
  "synthesis": "The three preprints share a computational strategy: recovering structural information from incomplete measurements using learned priors. cryoSENSE applies sparse and diffusion-based generative priors to compressive cryo-EM sensing, reconstructing protein images from undersampled data. AFM-Fold combines an equivariant CNN with guided diffusion to reconstruct 3D protein conformations from HS-AFM images, validated on both simulated and experimental data. The erythrocyte study uses a multi-fidelity neural network, trained on dissipative particle dynamics simulations, to reconstruct 3D shapes of normal and disease-related red blood cells from partial cross-sections. The new element across these items is the pairing of generative or simulation-informed priors with sparse or partial measurement modalities spanning electron microscopy, atomic force microscopy and cell morphology. Evidence here is limited to the listed abstracts; quantitative performance is not captured.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-20"
}
